              "(b) new ships of less than 24 metres (79 feet) in length ; (c) existing ships of less than 150 tons gross; (a) pleasure yachts not engaged in trade; (e) fishing vessels. (2) Nothing herein shall apply to ships solely navigating : (a) the Great Lakes of North America and the River St. Lawrence as far as a rhumb line drawn from Cap des Rosiers to West Point, Anticosti Island, and, on the north side of Anticosti Island, the meridian of longitude 63 W; (b) the Caspian Sea; (c) the Plate, Parana and Uruguay Rivers as far east as a rhumb line drawn between Punta Norte, Argentina, and Punta del Este, Uruguay."
